  "name": "Fear’s End",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/magic/control/hypnosis-mesmerism-eye.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A terror so deep that it grows into hopelessness. You can spend an action to expend six link depth from the link of a linked foe to force them to make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, they must spend their action making a weapon attack against themselves at advantage using their most powerful attack. This attack does not suffer from disadvantage due to being frightened. On a successful hit, the attack does critical damage and the target takes 100 psychic damage. On a successful saving throw, the target takes 50 psychic damage.</p><p><a href=\"https://dnd-wiki.org/wiki/Empath_(5e_Class)\">Source: Empath by Axis, co-authored by Ghostwheel</a> (CC BY-SA 3.0). See the module's AUTOMATION.md for what is automated and how rules are interpreted.</p>",
